Title: 0007-packed-city-fields
Repository: micropoliscore
Base-Commit: 69ccf87ed72d2d2950b70cf16ef1391439bd9d48
Requires: 0006-restore-saved-service-funding.patch
Author: aros-micropolis project
Date: 2026-09-17
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: Classic city file I/O on all engine platforms; fixes LP64 overwrites and alignment UB

Problem:
  On LP64, casting 16-bit history words to Quad reads and writes eight bytes for four-byte city fields, overwriting neighbors and using unaligned aliasing accesses.
Solution:
  Decode and encode explicit high/low 16-bit words with defined signed extension, independent of long width and host byte order.
Validation:
  tests/budget: 16 assertions pass with fatal host ASan/UBSan and on AROS One x86_64 ABIv11; direct four-byte disk fixture and adjacent-word regression. Seven-patch reproduction passes.
Removal:
  Permanent engine bug fix; remove local patch after adopting an upstream revision containing an equivalent fix.

